now because the way the scottish  elections work as we were discussing  uh where voters have got two votes it's  possible that alba does more damage to  the greens or even the conservatives and  labor than the snp  now the conservatives are so worried  about this their leader in scotland  douglas ross yesterday called for fellow  unionist parties to put aside their  differences  and form an alliance to stop a second  independence referendum douglas ross  joins us now and  firstly just your reaction to the kenny  mccaskill  interview he says this is all about  helping the snp building a super  majority do you think it will work that  way  well that's what it's all about for the  snp nationalists  i listened to every word from the alba  party representing  kenya mccaskill there and not once did  he mention covered recovery  or rebuilding up this pandemic  he didn't need to be fair well he didn't  speak about  recovery after this pandemic and how we  get scotland back up and running after  the last 12 months because for  nationalists  it's all about another independence  referendum and that's what i was saying  to  fellow unionist leaders here in scotland  yesterday we can't help the recovery we  can't rebuild scotland  when all the narrative from the scottish  government from the snp  and from the alba party it's going to be  focused on another independence  referendum so we've got to work together  to stop them  i'm interested in this you say you want  to work together with other  pro-unionists  and parties you've written to the labour  and the lib dem leaders  have they replied yet yes i mean sadly  they both turned down that offer but  the offer remains we've got to look at  how we approach this new threat  as you said in your introduction there  this is  could split the sm people but they don't  get many msps off the regional list so  it's more likely  to do more harm to the unionist party so  we've got to understand that threat  not ignore it and assume that we can  continue as normal  we've got to put our party politics to  one side in this important reference  effective referendum because the  nationalists want this election to be  about another  independence representative to separate  scotland from the rest of the uk  i'm just trying to work out what this  offer actually means  you know you want to work together with  other pro-unionist parties i mean are  you actually saying that you might go  into government a coalition government  if you like with labor  well that's one of the pledges that we  would sign up to a unionist manifesto if  the numbers work after the election to  work together  to get rid of the nationalists so you  would go into government with labour  i'm saying that's what we need to get  around the table and discuss because  after the last 14 years in scotland  for the snp have been in charge we've  not had the focus  on the economy on protecting jobs on  education and supporting nhs  we've had a focus on independence that's  the snp's priority  and the nationalist priority so we've  got to look at how we can build up  as big a coalition as possible to stop  that and  the speed at which the labour party and  the liberal democrats refused that offer  yesterday  tells me that we've got to just unite  behind the strongest opposition of the s  p then that's the scottish conservatives  i'm a bit confused because you say that  the problem with the snp  and the album party is that they want to  make the selection all about independent  independence rather than other issues  but surely by talking about and and  calling for  a pro-union alliance that is also making  the election all about independence  isn't it  well that's responding to the threat  that has now emerged that the alba party  have set up to work  with the scottish national party to get  super majority for independence  that means there will not be an  opportunity to discuss our recovery  not be an opportunity for the scottish  parliament to be laser focused on  rebuilding  after grouping because the nationalists  will drag us back to the same old  divisive destructive arguments of the  past  isn't the truth that actually making  this election all about independence  benefits the scottish conservatives  doesn't it you want to position yourself  as the most strongly pro-union party  we are the strongest pro union party in  scotland we've shown that  in the last election five years ago we  stopped the snp getting a majority  the scottish labour party so you want it  to be about independence don't you  no i want it to be about education in  scotland i wanted to be about protecting  jobs in scotland i wanted  to be about our recovery from this  pandemic as you heard from kenny  mccaskill  not a single word about recovery or  rebuilding from the alba party  for nationalists is all about  independence so you and you think you  can  choose or achieve all of those domestic  objectives most easily in coalition with  labour  well we've got to work with all parties  who want to stop the nationalists  they've been in power for a decade and a  half and look at what they've done in  scotland  nicholas sturgeon said judge her on her  number one priority  which would be education but of course  everyone can see her number one priority  has always been another independence  referendum and separating scotland from  the rest of the uk  we've got to wake up to this threat we  cannot continue to bury our heads in the  sun like the scottish labour party want  to do the threat is real  it's in front of us now let's place that  break and work together to stop the  nationalists otherwise scottish politics  will again be dominated by the  independence debate  if the next scottish parliament contains  the majority even a super majority for  independence will boris johnson just  refuse to grant a referendum in any  circumstances  well sadly that doesn't even matter to  the nationalists because they've said  they'll go ahead with a wildcat illegal  referendum enemy  so no matter what happens if you vote  for a nationalist party  get nicholas sturgeon's nationalists or  alex salmon's nationalist  their priority will be another  referendum whether it's a legal  referendum or an  illegal wildcat referendum they will not  be focused on recovery  they cannot be focused on rebuilding  scotland when they're trying to rip us  out of the united kingdom  the question i asked wasn't about what  the s p will do though is about what the  conservatives will do since you are you  know the leader of the scottish  conservatives  if there is a majority for independence  in the next scottish parliament  will boris johnson refuse to grant a  referendum  but that's the problem sophie that's  exactly the point i'm making it doesn't  matter  if it will or not though other people  can decide whether it matters people  want to know what it's going to do  yeah and the prime minister has been  clear he does not want another  independent referendum in scotland we  are in the middle of a pandemic we need  to focus on our recovery and rebuilding  but the nationalists will ignore that  the nationalists have already said and  nicolas sturgeon  set up a commission within the snp with  an 11-point plan  to have another independence referendum  even if it's an illegal  wildcat referendum without a section 30  order from the uk government  we know that boris johnson doesn't want  another referendum but will he refuse to  grant  another referendum in all circumstances  the prime minister has been clear he's  not going to grant  him the powers for another independence  referendum because he thinks it's  absolutely wrong for scotland right now  to be dragged back into that destructive  arguments of the past  to go through all the pain and suffering  that we had in scotland through that  last debate  we should be focused on recovery and  rebuilding but the nationals are going  to ignore that and they're going to say  we'll have a referendum anyway and that  will take scotland backwards rather than  focusing on our recovery  and rebuilding from this pandemic would  it be democratic though for boris  johnson to refuse to grant a referendum  if there is a majority  in favour of independence parties well  it wouldn't be democratic for the  nationalists to go ahead with a wildcat  legal referendum but they're going to do  it anyway  and this is the whole point this is why  i'm asking people to unite behind the  strongest party  to stop the snp and stop the  nationalists i'd like to do it with the  scottish labour party and the local  democrats  but if they're not up for that fight if  they can't see the threat in front of us  right now  and people have to see there is a party  that's willing to challenge the snp  willing to stand up to the nationalist  threat that we are facing here in  scotland  and that's the scottish conservatives we  stopped from five years ago we can do it  again  but the threat is very real it's in  front of us now we've got a short time  to stop them  and everyone has to back the strongest  party to stop the naturalist and that's  the scottish conservatives  okay thank you very much for being on  the program douglas ross thank you

